---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import SpinnerBuild from "../../components/UnderTheHood/SpinnerBuild.astro"
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components"
---

<TechniquePost slug="spinner-aria-busy">
  <section>
    <h2 id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A loading state is usually two things to keep in sync: a spinner element
      or class for sighted users, and <code>aria-busy</code> for assistive technology.
      Forget one and the two disagree.
    </p>
    <p>If the attribute is already there, it can be the only switch.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="the-trick">The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>[aria-busy="true"]</code> is the selector, no class and no extra element
      </li>
      <li>
        A <code>::before</code> circle with one transparent border side is the ring,
        {" "}<code>rotate(1turn)</code> in a <code>linear</code>, <code
          >infinite</code
        > loop spins it
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>1em</code> sizes it from the font and <code>currentColor</code> colors
        it from the text
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>:not(…)</code> skips form fields, <code>&lt;progress&gt;</code>,
        the root and anything with <code>aria-describedby</code>, such as a
        section pointing to its progress bar
      </li>
      <li><code>:not(:empty)</code> adds a gap only next to text</li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="css"
      code={`[aria-busy="true"]:not(input, select, textarea, html, progress, [aria-describedby]) {
  &::before {
    animation: spin 0.7s linear infinite;
    block-size: 1em;
    border: 3px solid;
    border-color: transparent currentColor currentColor;
    border-radius: 50%;
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    inline-size: 1em;
    opacity: 0.5;
    vertical-align: -0.14em;
  }

  &:not(:empty)::before {
    margin-inline-end: 0.5em;
  }
}

@keyframes spin {
  to {
    transform: rotate(1turn);
  }
}`}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
    <SpinnerBuild />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fallback">Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>:not()</code> with a selector list is Selectors Level 4. A browser without
        it drops the rule: no spinner, but <code>aria-busy</code> is still announced
      </li>
      <li>
        The animation isn't scaled by <code>--motion</code>, so it keeps
        spinning under reduced motion
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
